<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.041 percent from 10.060 percent at the previous auction on December 31.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p> Maturity date:		July 15, 1997 (July 1, 1997)</p>
<p> Average yield:		10.041 percent (10.060)</p>
<p> Value of bids accepted:   709.575 million (800.550 million)</p>
<p> Value of bids:		771.275 million (949.325 million)</p>
<p> Range accepted:	     9.900-10.090 percent (9.997-10.087)</p>
<p> Range of bids:		9.900-10.555 percent (9.997-10.400)</p>
<p> Number of bids accepted:  85 (60)</p>
<p> Number of bids:	     94 (79)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
